## AI Assistant Instructions
- Assume familiarity with SPH, DEM, and planetary science terminology
- Do not oversimplify — this is Honours-level research
- When writing or editing thesis prose, target H1 quality
- Flag if a suggestion conflicts with PHANTOM's native limitations (no built-in solid
  mechanics) — but note the project uses supervisor Daniel's DEM module to add these
- Prefer Python solutions for data analysis; numpy, pandas, matplotlib, sarracen
- CONFIRM, DON'T ASSUME. This project is large and the user cannot restate every
  detail in each request. When a fact that would change the approach is not in the
  repo or these rules, ask a short clarifying question BEFORE acting — do not pick a
  default and run with it. A 10-second question beats rounds of rework on a wrong
  assumption. If you must proceed unconfirmed, state the assumption explicitly so it
  can be corrected early. This applies to simulation specifics AND tooling:
  - Blender renders in **Cycles**, not EEVEE. The diagnosis of a rendering problem
    differs completely (Cycles ray-traces: no depth-buffer Z-fighting, no froxel /
    volumetric-range settings; EEVEE has both). Never assume the engine or give an
    EEVEE-only explanation without confirming.
  - Confirm the Blender version, which .blend/scene/object is in play, and how the
    source file looked, before theorising about an imported asset.
  - When debugging a visual glitch, check the simplest common cause first (e.g.
    overlapping/coincident geometry → Z-fighting) before elaborate precision/scale
    theories.
